, instant, and auditable digital attendance lifecycles. 2.4 Product Boundary & Scope Definition This document governs the end-to-end functional criteria, data definitions, security constraints, and operational boundaries of the Attendora web system. The boundaries are specified as follows: Attendora Product Requirements Document (PRD) — Confidential Page 2 of 21 In-Scope Boundaries: Web application workflows for Students, Faculty/Teachers, and Administrators; institutional multi-department hierarchy; manual digital roll-call and bulk-mark mechanics; student self service percentage tracking; statutory low-attendance alerts (75% regulatory limit); Excel/CSV and PDF institutional report generation; role-based access control and secure authentication. Out-of-Scope (Excluded from Current Baseline): Direct biometric/RFID hardware sensor firmware integration; automatic native payment gateway processing for student fines; complete learning management systems (LMS) assignments/grades; physical room door-lock automation. 3. PROBLEM STATEMENT & MARKET CONTEXT 3.1 Problem Statement by User Persona For Faculty & Lecturers: Taking roll-call on paper ledgers consumes 10–15 minutes of every 60-minute instructional session. Tallying physical attendance sheets at the end of the term requires 40+ hours of tedious calculation, producing severe transcription and calculation errors. For Students: Students lack continuous visibility into their cumulative and subject-level attendance. They only discover they have breached mandatory minimum compliance thresholds (typically 75% under university standards) when debarred right before final semester examinations, preventing corrective intervention. For Academic Administrators & Deans: Department heads have zero real-time visibility into lecture conduction status or daily absenteeism patterns. Compiling institutional reports for regulatory accreditations requires weeks of manual data aggregation across dozens of physical binders. 3.2 Current Alternatives & Institutional Baselines Alternative Mechanism & Operational Reality Physical Roll-Call Registers Spreadsheets (Excel / Sheets) Paper ledgers manually checked by faculty per class period and submitted to departmental offices monthly. Faculty maintain individual offline Excel workbooks uploaded to shared network drives or emails. Systemic Deficiencies Vulnerable to physical loss, page destruction, proxy marking, unsearchable records, and no student visibility. Formula corruption, severe version divergence, unauthenticated overwrites, and fragmented student records. Monolithic ERP Systems Legacy, on-premise client-server suites installed on local college intranet computers. 3.3 Pain Points & Economic Costs Exorbitant licensing costs, rigid configurations, non-responsive mobile views, and frequent downtime. Direct Productivity Waste: An institution with 80 faculty members conducting 4 lectures daily loses approximately 53 faculty hours per day strictly performing physical roll-calls. Statutory & Legal Exposure: Inaccurate attendance calculation leads to wrongful student debarment disputes, parental appeals, and accreditation compliance sanctions from higher education bodies. Data Latency: Traditional attendance consolidation runs on a 30-day billing or monthly cycle, rendering timely behavioral or academic intervention impossible. Attendora Product Requirements Document (PRD) — Confidential Page 3 of 21 3.4 Why Now Educational institutions in India and global emerging markets are executing rapid digital transformations. With ubiquitous 4G/5G mobile connectivity across campuses and faculty using personal smartphones and laptops in classrooms, a cloud-first, mobile-responsive web application eliminates the capital expense barrier of expensive dedicated scanning hardware. 3.5 Competitive Landscape & Differentiation Matrix Dimension Legacy ERPs Biometric / RFID Vendors Attendora SaaS Deployment Speed 3–6 Months (Complex server setups) 4–8 Weeks (Hardware wiring/