nce-shortage fines where applicable, but will not act as a credit card payment gateway or merchant account processor for student fees in MVP. 5. SUCCESS METRICS & KPIS 5.1 North Star Metric NORTH STAR METRIC: VERIFIED RECORDED STUDENT-LECTURES (VRSL) Definition: The total number of unique student-lecture sessions successfully recorded, validated, and finalized into the database per academic day. Strategic Justification: This metric captures core customer value across all three personas: faculty actively using the system, students receiving tracking entries, and institutions establishing regulatory audit trails. 5.2 Primary KPIs (AARRR Framework Aligned) Lifecycle Stage Key Performance Indicator Operational Definition Target Objective Acquisition Institution Roster Completion % of invited colleges uploading full student and faculty rosters within 7 days. > 80% onboarding completion Activation First-Lecture Execution Rate % of onboarded faculty who successfully mark their first digital lecture within 48h. > 85% activation Retention Weekly Active Faculty (WAF) Faculty logging in and submitting ≥ 4 lecture attendance rosters per week. > 92% sustained retention Engagement Student Portal Session Rate Average monthly logins per enrolled student reviewing status. > 4.0 sessions/month/student Quality / SLA Submission Error Rate Percentage of attendance submission API requests resulting in HTTP 5xx errors. < 0.05% of all submissions 5.3 Guardrail Metrics The engineering and product teams must track these metrics to ensure rapid product iteration does not degrade product integrity: Attendora Product Requirements Document (PRD) — Confidential Page 5 of 21 Data Revision Dispute Rate: Must remain below 0.2% of total attendance marks logged (ensures teacher accuracy and low tampering). Critical Path API Latency: 95th percentile latency for roll-call submission must stay < 500ms on standard 3G/4G connections. System Availability: Core service uptime must maintain a strict 99.9% ava