ng any internal route are redirected to /login with 302 code. 2. Students attempting to access /faculty/* or /admin/* routes receive HTTP 403 Forbidden with zero data leaked. 3. Faculty attempting to access /admin/* receive HTTP 403 Forbidden. 4. User session state is validated on every server transaction. FR-AUTH-03 Session Expiry & Secure Logout P0 1. User sessions expire after 8 hours of inactivity. 2. Clicking "Log Out" invalidates the server-side session token immediately. 3. Browser back-navigation post-logout displays login screen and does not display cached private data. FR-AUTH-04 Password Reset Workflow P1 1. User enters registered email; system sends cryptographically random, single-use reset token valid for 30 minutes. 2. Token expires immediately upon successful password update. 3. Passwords must enforce minimum 8 characters with at least 1 number and 1 special symbol. Attendora Product Requirements Document (PRD) — Confidential Page 9 of 21 9.2 Module: Faculty Operations & Attendance Marking (FAC) Req ID Feature Description Priority Testable Acceptance Criteria FR-FAC-01 Lecture Session Creation P0 1. Faculty selects Department, Class/Semester, Section, and assigned Subject from dropdowns. 2. Date defaults to current calendar day; lecture time-slot defaults to current hour. 3. System validates that the faculty member is officially assigned to teach the selected subject. 4. Duplicate lecture prevention: If a lecture record exists for the exact same subject, section, date, and hour, system prompts confirmation: "A lecture already exists for this slot. Overwrite or create extra session?" FR-FAC-02 Interactive Digital Roll Call Sheet P0 1. System dynamically renders table containing all active enrolled students sorted by Roll Number. 2. Every student displays: Roll Number, Full Name, and a toggleable status badge. 3. "Mark All Present" default: All toggles initialize in "Present" state. 4. Single tap/click on student row flips state to "Absent" (highlighte