oses, late admissions), the system must handle exceptions predictably. Attendora Product Requirements Document (PRD) — Confidential Page 12 of 21 Failure Scenario Underlying Condition / Trigger Prescribed System Behavior & Recovery Mid-Roll-Call Network Drop Teacher marks 40 students; device loses internet connectivity before hitting "Submit". Client-side local storage retains toggled states. UI alerts: "Connection lost. Changes cached locally. Do not close tab." Auto-retries submission when connection restores. Concurrent Double Submission Teacher accidentally double-taps the "Confirm Submit" button rapidly on mobile. Client disables submit button immediately on first tap (idempotency key generated). Backend validates unique combination of (SubjectID + SectionID + Date + Slot); second request is rejected gracefully. Student Added Mid Semester A student joins class in week 6 after 20 lectures have already been conducted. Admin enrolls student with an "Enrollment Effective Date". Attendance calculation formula ignores lectures conducted prior to effective date; student is not penalized for prior sessions. Zero Lectures Conducted (Div/0) New semester starts; student or subject dashboard loaded before any attendance is logged. System detects Total Conducted == 0. Percentage displays "N/A" or "100.0% (No classes held)"; prevents division by-zero application crashes. Unauthorized Direct URL Probe Student attempts typing /admin/export-defaulters directly into browser bar. Backend auth middleware intercepts request, confirms absence of Admin claims, logs security warning event, and issues HTTP 403 redirect to /student/dashboard. Corrupt CSV Ingestion Admin uploads a CSV file containing 500 rows, but row 42 has a missing email and row 108 has an invalid character. Atomic transaction dry-run: System processes zero writes, displays validation error modal showing exact row numbers and issues ("Row 42: Email missing"), and prompts re-upload. 11. KEY USER FLOWS 11.1 Primary Facu