6.2 Security Boundaries & Threat Mitigations





Tenant Isolation Breach Prevention: Even if an application bug omits WHERE tenant_id = ..., PostgreSQL RLS policies evaluate the active session variable app.current_tenant_id at the database kernel level and return zero records for cross-tenant attempts.



Session Hijacking Mitigation: Short-lived 15-minute access tokens minimize exposure. Immediate token revocation is supported via a high-performance Redis Deny-List (SET blacklist:jti:<uuid> EX 900).



Input Hygiene: Strict Pydantic models validate all incoming payloads prior to domain dispatch, blocking SQL injection, parameter tampering, and cross-site scripting attempts.

