8. Reliability, Observability & Operational Resilience

8.1 Resilience Controls





Circuit Breaker Pattern: Integrated around third-party API gateways (SendGrid/Twilio/Razorpay). If failures exceed 50% over a 60-second window, the circuit trips to OPEN, instantly routing fallback messages to a pending retry table and preventing web worker thread starvation.



Database Connection Stability: Managed via PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode. This prevents connection saturation when application instances scale out during morning attendance peak windows (08:30 AM – 10:30 AM).



Idempotent Write Safety: Attendance session submission endpoints require a client-generated UUID idempotency key (Idempotency-Key: <uuid>). Duplicate requests caused by erratic network retries return the original cached response without re-executing writes.

